The paper 'Attention Is All You Need' uses positional encoding to handle word order without recurrence. Specifically, it relies on the use of sine and cosine wave functions to encode the position of the token into the embedding, as shown in the equations:

{\displaystyle PE_{({\rm {pos}},2i)}=\sin({\rm {pos}}/{10000}^{2i/d_{\rm {model}}})}

{\displaystyle PE_{({\rm {pos}},2i+1)}=\cos({\rm {pos}}/{10000}^{2i/d_{\rm {model}}})}

This method allows the model to process all tokens in parallel while preserving the order information.
